<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">CERN</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as European Organization for Nuclear Research</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">CERN, the European Organization for Nuclear Research, is an intergovernmental particle physics laboratory founded in 1954 on the Franco-Swiss border near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>. It operates the world's largest particle accelerators, including the Large Hadron Collider, with which the Higgs boson was discovered in 2012. The World Wide Web was invented there by Tim Berners-Lee in 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cern.jpg" alt="CERN" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Organization for Nuclear Research Organisation européenne pour la recherche nucléaire · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CERN_logo_badge.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
